{0 odoc Example}

This is an example odoc documentation page used for testing.

{1 Basic Formatting}

Text can be {b bold}, {i italic}, or {e emphasised}.
You can also use {^ superscript} and {_ subscript}.

Code spans look like [List.map] and escape sequences like \{ and \}.

{1 Code Blocks}

A simple code block:

{[
let x = 1 + 2
let () = print_int x
]}

A code block with language tag:

{@ocaml[
let greet name =
  Printf.printf "Hello, %s!\n" name
]}

{1 Verbatim}

{v
This is verbatim text.
  Whitespace is preserved.
    Exactly as written.
v}

{1 Math}

Inline math: {m x^2 + y^2 = r^2}

Block math:

{math \sum_{i=0}^{n} i = \frac{n(n+1)}{2}}

{1 References and Links}

A reference: {!List.map}

A reference with text: {{!List.map} the map function}

A link: {:https://ocaml.org}

A link with text: {{:https://ocaml.org} the OCaml website}

{1 Lists}

Heavy unordered list:

{ul
{- First item}
{- Second item}
{- Third item}
}

Heavy ordered list:

{ol
{- Step one}
{- Step two}
{li Step three}
}

Light list:

- First item
- Second item
+ Nested item

{1 Headings}

{2 Level Two}

{3 Level Three}

{3:my-anchor Heading with Anchor}

{1 Tables}

Heavy table:

{table
{tr
  {th Header 1}
  {th Header 2}
}
{tr
  {td Cell 1}
  {td Cell 2}
}
}

{1 Tags}

@author Jane Doe
@since 1.0.0
@version 2.0
@deprecated
@param x the input value
@return the computed result
@raise Not_found when the key is missing
@see <https://ocaml.org> for more information

